Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions regulates algorithmic recommendation services and requires services to implement guidelines and provisions including:

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions establish management systems and technical measures for algorithm examination, user registration, information dissemination, security monitoring, incident response, data protection, and fraud prevention;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions conduct regular assessments of algorithms, models, data and application outcomes;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions strengthen information security management and identify unlawful/harmful information;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions implement tactics to avoid user harms and prohibit dissemination of misinformation;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions ban false account registration, trading, manipulation and anti-competitive practices;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions implement specific guidelines for services targeting minors, the elderly, workers and consumers;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions implement transparent and efficient complaint handling processes;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions establishes graded/categorized algorithm management system and filing procedures for relevant department authorities charged with oversight of algorithmic recommendation services;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions authorizes relevant departments to carry out security assessments and inspections and;

Internet Information Service Algorithmic Recommendation Management Provisions specifies legal liabilities and penalties for violations.
